    "killington": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Killington",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-24 16:22:33",
      "note": "Good evening, Killington Family, It’s officially the weekend. Time to pack the car and head to The Beast for what’s shaping up to be one of the best spring weekends ever! Friday was marked by plenty of sunshine, warm temps later in the day, and a whole lot of smiles. There’s more of that in store tomorrow. Temps are dropping into the high 20s tonight and should break 32 degrees within the first hour of the day. It’s going to rise into the mid 40s tomorrow, and the sun will be shining high in the sky all day long, making for a picture-perfect spring day. Surfaces should be a bit variable in the morning thanks to wintry temps tonight, with conditions consisting of machined groomed hardpack and frozen granular to start the day. As temperatures rise and the sun works it's spring magic, the snow should soften back to that buttery corn we love by the afternoon. Our grooming team is running it back tonight, smoothing out Superstar, Skyelark, Lower Bittersweet, and surrounding areas. If you’re looking to carve up some turns on a freshly groomed surface, get out early, as the bumps are bound to return by the afternoon. The sun should make for irresistible spring conditions later in the day. Put on your SPF and enjoy it out there! Our kparks crew cooked up five features in Skyehawk earlier this week for all your spring park needs. Just drop down Superstar’s headwall and hang a right to find yourself at the top. We’ll keep the park alive as long as conditions allow. Thank you, Park Crew! The Superstar Six is scheduled to spin starting at 8:00 a.m. and will be open until 5:00 p.m. on Saturday for some late laps. Please note that there is no longer any beginner terrain available, and late season conditions will continue to exist in some locations. On Saturday, the vibes are going to be all time at the Superstar Umbrella Bar as we kick off Decked Out Days . It's a retro-themed celebration of spring with a live DJ set from Benny Shreds, games, NÜTRL giveaways, and much more. Best dressed from the 80s era wins a prize! There's nothing like spring at The Beast. See you out there! – Austin Operating Day: 165 Season passes for 26/27 are now on sale! Lock in the lowest price on Beast 365 or Winter Unlimited passes with lots of perks, plus free skiing & riding for the rest of this spring. And there's more good news for families: Youth & Child pass pricing has been significantly reduced for next season, with over $300 in savings available on Beast 365 access. Lifts The Superstar Six will operate seven days a week from 9:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Monday through Friday, from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. on Saturdays, and from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Sundays. Starting on May 3rd, the Superstar Six will be open Friday through Sunday while conditions allow. The Tubing Park presented by bubly is closed for the season. Uphill Travel Uphill travel is now closed for this season. Please visit killington.com/uphill for full information on our uphill travel policies. MOUNTAIN SERVICES Parking & Shuttles Parking is available at our K-1 Lodge and at the top of Killington Road. Vale Road is closed on Saturday mornings to facilitate Snowdon Triple chair pickups. Please respect signage and allow our parking staff to assist you on your trip to the slopes. Shuttle service is available from 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. midweek and 6:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends and holidays through Sunday, May 3rd unless otherwise stated in this report. Winter car camping and overnight parking is only available in the lot across from Skyeship Lodge, though please note that the Skyeship Lodge is closed for the season. See details here . Lodge Services All lodges listed here are open daily from 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekdays and 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends/peak dates*. K-1 Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on weekdays and 7:30 a.m. on weekends/peak dates. Lunch: Served from 10:30 a.m. - 2:00 p.m. on weekdays and from 10:30 a.m. - 3:00 p.m. on weekends, with limited grill station offerings midweek. Brew Bar (2nd floor): Closed for the season. Will re-open during the weekend dependent on weather conditions. K-1 Pub (3rd floor): Closed for the season. Rentals & Killington Sports at K-1: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Killington Sports will close at 12:00 p.m. on Tuesday, April 21st for inventory purposes. Demos & Tuning: Available via the K-1 Rental Shop daily through May 3rd. Beast 365, Unlimited, and Midweek Pass holders can receive 50% off demo rentals. Guest Services: 1st floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 1:00 p.m. on weekdays and until 4:30 p.m. on weekends/peak dates. 2nd floor location is closed for the season. Superstar Umbrella Bar: Open at 11:00 a.m. from Friday - Sunday offering beer, wine, liquor, and specialty hot cocktails. Ramshead Lodge - Closed for the season. Bear Mountain Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Demos & Tuning remains open seven days a week, providing tuning services for guests and Season Tune holders. Demos also available with more options at K-1. Skyeship Lodge - Closed for the season. On-Mountain Dining Options : Peak Lodge – Closed for the season. Jerk Jamaican Mountain Grill – Closed for the season. Ledgewood Yurt – Closed for the season. Mountain services are subject to change. Please check here daily before making your lunch and lodge choices. Winter Lift Tickets and rentals must be purchased online at this link . Check to see if your pass is good to go using our Online Pass Checker . Find our Season Pass FAQs by clicking here . Season passes for summer 2026 and winter 26/27 are now on sale! Buy now . Have a ticketing question? Our text number ( 802-523-2202 ) is the best way to get it answered quickly, but please note that we cannot process transactions via text. Have a season pass question? Call 1-800-621-MTNS or email seasonpass@killington.com Please visit Killington.com/cancellation for more details on our cancellation policy. Killington is a cashless resort. We accept all major credit cards as well as Apple, Google, and Samsung Pay. *No remaining Peak Dates during winter 2025/26. We strive to have the most up-to-date and accurate snow report, but errors can happen from time to time. If you have feedback or a correction for us, please share it here.",
